  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "FoMEMO: Towards Foundation Models for Expensive Multi-objective Optimization addresses the challenge of efficiently performing multi-objective optimization in real-world scenarios. MiniOpt: Reasoning to Model and Solve General Optimization Problems with Limited Resources provides a lightweight, efficient approach to achieving optimization generalization across diverse optimization problems.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "FoMEMO (Foundation Models for Expensive Multi-objective Optimization) proposes a decomposition-based training paradigm to convert multi-objective optimization into preference-wise aggregated posterior learning tasks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "MiniOpt (Reasoning to Model and Solve General Optimization Problems with Limited Resources) uses a reasoning-to-model-and-solve paradigm and a two-stage training framework with RLVR to achieve efficient optimization generalization.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both models demonstrate strong performance in diverse optimization benchmarks while requiring fewer parameters and training data than existing learning-based methods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
